<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The layout the ResHook case replaces. The tag is the first half of the payload: after a
    replacement the inflated root must carry the module's tag instead of this one, which is
    observable without reading a single id out of either package's resource table.

    The id is the other half. The module's copy declares the same name, so the reference inside it
    has to be translated to the number this package gave it here; nothing else in this file is
    inflated once the replacement is in place.

    This is the only place the target declares an id, and that is load-bearing: aapt2 numbers the
    entries of a type in name order, so probe_root is entry 0 here while the module has a name
    ahead of it. Adding an id that sorts before probe_root would give both packages the same number
    for it, and the case would report SETUP rather than measure a rewrite it can no longer see. The
    attribute the replacement carries is declared in values/attrs.xml for the same reason; it is
    deliberately not used here, since this document is the one being replaced.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/probe_root"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:tag="ORIGINAL"
    android:text="original" />
